---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '~/components/PageHeader.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '~/config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What Mindful collects (nothing on purpose), which outside services your browser talks to, and what Cloudflare sees as our host."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[52rem]">
    <PageHeader title="How we treat your visit." crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} />

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Mindful is a static website of essays. There are no accounts, no sign-up forms, no comments,
        no analytics, no advertising and no tracking scripts. The site sets no cookies and does not
        write anything to <code>localStorage</code> or <code>sessionStorage</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>Cloudflare, our host</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served by Cloudflare, which also runs DNS for our domain. Every request you make
        to mindful.engg.app goes through Cloudflare. Like any web host, it processes standard
        request data to deliver and protect the site: your IP address, the page or file you asked
        for, the time, your browser&rsquo;s user agent and the referring page. Cloudflare may keep
        this in its request logs. What it collects and how long it keeps it is covered by
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare&rsquo;s privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Images from Picsum</h2>
      <p>
        The photos at the top of essays are placeholder images from
        <a href="https://picsum.photos/">Picsum</a>. Your browser loads them from
        <code>picsum.photos</code>, which redirects to <code>fastly.picsum.photos</code>. Every page
        also tells the browser to open a connection to those two hosts early, so they can see your
        IP address and user agent even on pages without a photo. No other third-party host is
        contacted when you read the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Fonts</h2>
      <p>
        Fraunces and Newsreader are bundled with the site from Fontsource packages and served by
        Cloudflare with everything else. No request goes to Google Fonts or any other font service.
      </p>

      <h2>Offline copies on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Mindful registers a small service worker so pages you have visited, and the site&rsquo;s own
        styles, scripts, fonts and images, can be cached in your browser. That cache is how the
        offline page works. It stays on your device; we never see it. Clearing site data in your
        browser removes it.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        Some pages link elsewhere, for example to a helpline directory or to our code on GitHub.
        Those sites are only contacted if you follow the link, and their own privacy policies apply
        once you are there.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Mindful is written for adults. We collect nothing from anyone, children included.</p>

      <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
      <p>
        If the hosting or anything else on this page changes, we will update the page. To ask a
        question or report a problem, open an issue on
        <a href={siteConfig.issuesUrl}>the Mindful repository on GitHub</a>. The rules for using the
        site are in the <a href="/terms">Terms of use</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
